{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why","id":863271,"title":"Beasts and Demons together - Why?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-10T12:41:36-07:00","id":863271,"title":"Beasts and Demons together - Why?","content":"Exactly. As the titles say. Why would a Demon and a Beast(Or multiple of said instances) stick together for a longer period of time? As far as I can tell, neither side has anything to offer to the second that couldn't be achieved from another source, and their mutual attitudes towards each other are like water and oil. So what would happen to bring them together. It doesn't have to be a friendly relationship, but one lasting longer than a single operation. Any ideas from you guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:41:01-07:00","id":863301,"title":"","content":"AH! I love this topic!<br /> <br /> Let me eat lunch, I'll get right back to it.<br /> <br /> (Preview: I have hopes of working Kung Fury and Triceracops into it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:42:47-07:00","id":863361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863301#post863301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Preview: I have hopes of working Kung Fury and Triceracops into it)</div> </div> </div> </div>[Breathing intensifies]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T16:12:44-07:00","id":863368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863301#post863301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AH! I love this topic!<br /> <br /> Let me eat lunch, I'll get right back to it.<br /> <br /> (Preview: I have hopes of working Kung Fury and Triceracops into it)</div> </div> </div> </div>My wife and I must have been the only two people who didn't like <i>Kung Fury</i>.<br /> <br /> That being said, Demons and Beasts don't have any baked-in reasons to help each other out. So it comes down to story-specific favors and such. However, since Demons have the best abilities to pretend to be non-supernaturals (yay Spoofing) they could perform intel-gathering for the Beast. If a Beast doesn't have Eyes of Heaven then a Demon's spy abilities can be used to get what a Beast might need to feed on a target.<br /> <br /> Beasts can give Demons something in return for this favor: somebody who can do jobs for them without the Demon having to risk their Cover, somebody who can keep an eye out for other supernatural creatures, that sort of thing. Basically a fixer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T17:13:20-07:00","id":863390,"title":"","content":"Okay, so.<br /> <br /> Why would a Beast and a Demon work together?<br /> <br /> In the entire vein of Beast's crossover elements and it's many implications and questions, Demon is perhaps one of the more interesting one simply because it was the one time Beast gave a hard &quot;NO&quot; on the subject. As I brought up in another response, there's a lot of reasons for this, although I would mainly argue that it comes down to the fact that, on a thematic level, the God-Machine embodies everything that mankind has done to defeat Beasts in the most meaningful sense. Civilization diminishes the primordial fears, and the God-Machine has it's radio waves all up in all corners of civilization-in fact, it wouldn't be unfair to say that the fear of the God-Machine is the fear of it eliminating fear and desire, the two things that drive Beasts.<br /> <br /> But if you're paying a modicum of attention, you'll notice I said God-Machine, not Demon, and while on a cosmological level the two are tied together, on a thematic level, the greatest irony is that demons and Beasts actually fill somewhat similar niches, just facing different directions, with Beast's reducing to the past and demons subverting towards the future. And that already creates a unique precedence for some settings, where in the two work together against the God-machine for their own reasons. Is that the only way? No, and a little digging brings up a few points that ensure that Beasts and Demons can avoid the catastrophe of cats and dogs, but even do it in the long term.<br /> <br /> Yeah. Beasts and Demons can be friends for the long term. We're going crazy here.<br /> <br /> So, what's the first way this can happen? Well...<br /> <br /> <b>1) The Beast doesn't push the search key.</b><br /> <br /> Admittedly, this one is unlikely to happen because a big part of Beast's instincts and incentives relate to seeking out and drawing from the presence and experiences of other monsters. So, because it's a violation of a Beast's general gaming direction, we won't dwell here-but it's worth noting that the thing that usually sets Beasts and demons at each other's throats is a Beast using Family Resemblance on the demon and winning to some degree. If a Beast can avoid doing that and dropping Shaken or Leveraged on one of them, and instead they come to a knowledge of one another's nature the long way around, this could easily set the stage for an easier relationship. Long and tedious, sure, but that's how most people work.<br /> <br /> <b>2) For the Cute Murderpuppy We Call Fenris-Ur</b><br /> <br /> The most common reason for them to start working together is because they have ties to the same person, and in fact that can lead to a long relationship that increases a likelihood of them coming together to share totally radical fistbumps. And it's not even all that unusual, particularly since they do have motives to seek out the same kind of persons. Beasts inherently follow their own pack instinct in seeking out other monsters, but a demon does have reason to seek out the other monsters as well and establish good working relationships of some kind, since other monsters don't tip the angels off as easily. That's a huge advantage for any demon, and it's one they would totally try and take advantage of. This kind of seeking often leads to the same places, and it also quickly reveals the value of the Beast to the demon, because a demon will doubtless see how the Beast makes everyone else more effective. Meanwhile, a Best is likely to hang out with and work with a demon for no other reason than their family members do so as well. Naturally, this involves a lot of time working things out, but sheer repetition and reliability means that their propinquity is likely to increase one way or the other.<br /> <br /> <b>3) Rage Against the Teachers, The Parents, and, oh yeah, The Machine</b><br /> <br /> Neither Beasts nor demons have an instinctive liking for systems in the world. Demons might be able to take advantage of the systems for the purposes of hiding, but almost all of them recognize it as the imposition, if not subjugation, of malefic forces from on high. Beasts hearken back to the primal days without all this order, nevermind how the current system favors Heroes trying to one-up Beasts in brutal and violent ways. Really, it wouldn't be surprising to find Beasts and demons protesting the same Trump rally, or participating in the same riot. Their reasons are different, but things like anarchy, freedom of expression, the chasing of taboos-all this counter-cultural stuff is bound to attract them, and where there's common complaints, there's common cause which leads to allegiances, and allegiances can lead to camaraderie.<br /> <br /> <b>4) Across this Beautiful World</b><br /> <br /> Beasts and Demons are unique in that they both have the greatest ability to travel between all the worlds. Now, granted, Demons only have that in the form of a God-machine alerting Exploit, so it's not intrinsic to them, but they are the only one to have a tool that lets them go to any other plane in existence-and as world walkers go, the company is a little lonely, before even talking about all the problems where it pays to have someone at your back without having the same tools as you. On this elite but broad road through worlds, demons and Beasts are likely to be one another's only consistent companions, and while hanging with your own is fine, in the end, the road has it's own demands, and travellers never know who they'll end up with. What were once begrudging souls caught in the same ravine can easily turn into a caravan of friendship, dreams, and bloody, bloody murder.<br /> <br /> And that's just a few things. The key thing to remember is that the deck is stacked against them, but it's not prohibiting. If monster's personalities click, well, just like with people, they'll find reasons to work with one another anyways. And in the end, they might just end up being the best damned partners they ever had, going back in time to save each other because, dammit, they love each other.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, that was pretty damn weak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-10-2016, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T18:46:33-07:00","id":863419,"title":"","content":"I still find it a little odd that Demons are arbitrarily excluded from kinship with Beasts. I get that supposedly being of the God Machine is mutually exclusive with being of the Dark Mother, but it feels contradictory with the otherwise broad and modular take on the setting. If you're going to include everything else excluding Demons doesn't feel right, and seems to mostly come down to the developer pushing one specific cosmology in an area where it doesn't really make a whole lot of sense. <br /> <br /> At my table Demons are kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T19:51:51-07:00","id":863447,"title":"","content":"It's not arbitrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T20:00:04-07:00","id":863451,"title":"","content":"The long answer would take an essay I don't much care to write at this point, so the long and short of it is that both thematically and by the implied cosmology of Demon, all things God-Machine and such basically are not a part of the world that Beast's can interact with. These decisions help to cement the feel and themes of each one respectively. One way or another, angels and demons are sacred, profane, and <i>always</i> <i>apart.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T21:24:46-07:00","id":863474,"title":"","content":"Also, the Tempters would definitely see the potential in hiring Beasts as diplomatic allies when interacting with other supernaturals. Besides Thicker Than Water, Family Resemblance and Mother's Kiss, the Tempters could make use all the Social Merits that the more outgoing Beasts accumulate in exchange for lending/selling their own Social Merits gained through Pacts and such. If the Tempter in question is lucky, he can even hire a Beast with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/734872-homebrew-idea-new-type-of-family-dinner?p=787169#post787169\"><b>Find A Vein.</b></a><br /> <br /> Like Arc said, the Beast can use Skeleton Key and the Demon can use Rip The Gates to explore the four main Invisible Realms together, and likely more. <br /> <br /> Tempters would do this for the sake of finding new business partners and resources to turn into products. The big attraction here are the Goblin Markets, but there's a lot more. For example: hiring spirits as spies/hidden security and convincing Kerberoi to guard your Pact documents. If the Demon has Show Of Power, all the different supernatural powers he has seen firsthand can be turned into a Gadget through that Exploit, essentially letting him sell bootleg Tokens and such. The Beast partner can share in the profits, or just enjoy the exploration and Feeding for their own sake.<br /> <br /> Inquisitors would do this for the sake of gathering intel and keeping an eye on possible threats before they can cross into the baseline realm. <br /> <br /> Saboteurs could have more pragmatic partnerships along the lines of &quot;I take care of this Hero, you help me bring down this Infrastructure&quot;. As the Saboteur and Beast prove their skills and reliability to each other, they can become fellow warriors of one type or another. Plus, the right Lairs make for incredible training rooms, obstacle courses, firing ranges and so on.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I don't know how Integrators could benefit from having a Beast around. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-11-2016, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T21:33:15-07:00","id":863477,"title":"","content":"And now this is making me wonder what kind of holy abomination would ensue if a Demon and a Beast had a child together; Beast has no minor splat as far as I know, so at most we could expect it to have the general child-of-a-Demon splat, but if their child also became a Beast and retained its connection to the God-Machine in some way...or would that immediately send red flags in the God-Machine, that something that primordial has access to its tools?<br /> <br /> I dunno, sounds like a really interesting thing, especially since, barring a long and friendship inspiring journey, this sort of thing really could unite a Beast and a Demon; the human aspect of the child appreciates the Beast's nature easier than a Demon would, but the child would also appreciate the problems that a Demon faces regularly. Add into the fact that this child has two very different cosmologies on demand if they're ever in danger and...yeah, I can see them a force to be reconned with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T21:48:26-07:00","id":863485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863477#post863477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now this is making me wonder what kind of holy abomination would ensue if a Demon and a Beast had a child together; Beast has no minor splat as far as I know, so at most we could expect it to have the general child-of-a-Demon splat, but if their child also became a Beast and retained its connection to the God-Machine in some way...or would that immediately send red flags in the God-Machine, that something that primordial has access to its tools?<br /> <br /> I dunno, sounds like a really interesting thing, especially since, barring a long and friendship inspiring journey, this sort of thing really could unite a Beast and a Demon; the human aspect of the child appreciates the Beast's nature easier than a Demon would, but the child would also appreciate the problems that a Demon faces regularly. Add into the fact that this child has two very different cosmologies on demand if they're ever in danger and...yeah, I can see them a force to be reconned with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a weird scenario in my head, because while a Heir can apparently Awaken or First Change, the connotations are the the infrastructure that allows an Heir to be an Heir is always there. The Devouring challenges this notion somewhat in that even those few Beasts who have a Horror innately still undergo a radical spiritual metamorphosis, to such a point that it seems likely the infrastructure would break.<br /> <br /> Even more terrifying, though, is the idea of it sticking. Remember that Beast's Horrors are shards of the collective soul of humanity. Introducing an Heir's Cipher onto that seems like a <i>terrible</i> idea.<br /> <br /> In short, someone needs to roleplay this out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T22:24:03-07:00","id":863490,"title":"","content":"I recall it was mentioned somewhere ,though it might have just been hypothesizing on the forums, aren't Beasts inviable targets for a Demon's pact? If that's accurate then a Beast would be one of the rare allies a Demon could have that couldn't be easily replaced. If not then a Beast's ability to detect other supernaturals would probably come in handy for knowing how to handle negotiations and avoiding the burn that comes from a soul pact with a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T23:04:58-07:00","id":863495,"title":"","content":"It's in the book that a Beast can't make a pact with a Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T23:22:01-07:00","id":863498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863419#post863419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it a little odd that Demons are arbitrarily excluded from kinship with Beasts. I get that supposedly being of the God Machine is mutually exclusive with being of the Dark Mother, but it feels contradictory with the otherwise broad and modular take on the setting. If you're going to include everything else excluding Demons doesn't feel right, and seems to mostly come down to the developer pushing one specific cosmology in an area where it doesn't really make a whole lot of sense.<br /> <br /> At my table Demons are kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that being kin to a beast, who aren't kin to normal humans, or animals, or objects, would mean the beasts would lower the demon's cover faster than the ball drops at New Year's Eve, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863485#post863485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more terrifying, though, is the idea of it sticking. Remember that Beast's Horrors are shards of the collective soul of humanity. Introducing an Heir's Cipher onto that seems like a <i>terrible</i> idea.<br /> <br /> In short, someone needs to roleplay this out.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or better yet, use the Nephilim from the Demon's storytellers guide. The correlation between nephilim and giant is a thing in the folklore, after all.<br /> <br /> And the idea of a nephilim beast powering their demonic transformations through sating their hunger, would mean that they're probably less a problem for themselves (no turning themselves into protoplasmic goo through integrity breaks), and more an issue for everyone else. <br /> <br /> If memory serves there is a version in which the flood was really about getting rid of the giants/nephilim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-11-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T05:49:17-07:00","id":863583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863451#post863451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way or another, angels and demons are sacred, profane, and <i><b>always</b></i> <i><b>apart</b>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I disliked on their innate strife with one another or needed convincing, but...<i>whoa</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:22:18-07:00","id":863623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863451#post863451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The long answer would take an essay I don't much care to write at this point, so the long and short of it is that both thematically and by the implied cosmology of Demon, all things God-Machine and such basically are not a part of the world that Beast's can interact with. These decisions help to cement the feel and themes of each one respectively. One way or another, angels and demons are sacred, profane, and <i>always</i> <i>apart.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it comes down to whether you give primacy to the theme of Demon's separateness or the theme of Beast's kinship. Obviously you, and the the developers, are in the former camp. I find better story potential in the latter though, so that's how I prefer to run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T10:09:22-07:00","id":863742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863623#post863623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose it comes down to whether you give primacy to the theme of Demon's separateness or the theme of Beast's kinship.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Primacy&quot; here meaning &quot;the ability to decide whether a non-Demon splat gets to answer the question of what Demon's central aggressively-mundane supernatural force is and also provide an easy route to a quarter of the game's typical manifestations of its titular long-term goal.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The theme of Beast's kinship&quot; takes the view that the other never-even-thought-they-were-human splat the Begotten can interact with is the adopted child of the family. Power and change are old as all get out. Meanwhile, there's nothing primordial about the tax code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:54:31-07:00","id":863804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863583#post863583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I disliked on their innate strife with one another or needed convincing, but...<i>whoa</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I have been saying those exact words for years, so it's a little weird to see a reaction to them now.<br /> <br /> Still, glad it triggered a new layer of appreciation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:31:41-07:00","id":865297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=863485#post863485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a weird scenario in my head, because while a Heir can apparently Awaken or First Change, the connotations are the the infrastructure that allows an Heir to be an Heir is always there. The Devouring challenges this notion somewhat in that even those few Beasts who have a Horror innately still undergo a radical spiritual metamorphosis, to such a point that it seems likely the infrastructure would break.<br /> <br /> Even more terrifying, though, is the idea of it sticking. Remember that Beast's Horrors are shards of the collective soul of humanity. Introducing an Heir's Cipher onto that seems like a <i>terrible</i> idea.<br /> <br /> In short, someone needs to roleplay this out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the way I'd handle this in my games would be to make it so that the Heir would go through their Devouring and find themselves rather unique among the Beasts. I would make it so that they could have kinship with demons and the like instead of the other supernaturals. I could even see something like that as the origin of a new Family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:45:39-07:00","id":865301,"title":"","content":"Again, that's terrifying. If Beasts can access those marked or made by the God-Machine, the God-Machine can do that in reverse, and that screams &quot;end of humanity&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> Demons being able to directly interface with Beasts isn't exactly a picnic either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:56:08-07:00","id":865399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=865301#post865301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that's terrifying. If Beasts can access those marked or made by the God-Machine, the God-Machine can do that in reverse, and that screams &amp;quot;end of humanity&amp;quot; to me.<br /> <br /> Demons being able to directly interface with Beasts isn't exactly a picnic either.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something that the machine probably has an interest in experimenting with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:27:30-07:00","id":865513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why?p=865301#post865301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that's terrifying. If Beasts can access those marked or made by the God-Machine, the God-Machine can do that in reverse, and that screams &amp;quot;end of humanity&amp;quot; to me.<br /> <br /> Demons being able to directly interface with Beasts isn't exactly a picnic either.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right. It is terrifying. Such an individual would need to be kept out of the grasp of the God Machine at all costs. There's a great reason for demons and Beasts to work together. Both sides would be invested in keeping the living McGuffin from becoming the God Machine's back door into the collective dreams of mankind. ...I think I need to go design this for a chronicle at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T17:13:48-07:00","id":867933,"title":"","content":"The only problem with the child of a beast and a demon is like fractals some would rather they were dead than risk the machine getting their hands on them. But I do think it'd be interesting if, as it's been said, that unlocked kinship with demons. <br /> <br /> As to why demons and beasts would work together I feel that can boil down to a &quot;it's just business&quot; type relationship. Each has something the other doesn't. If a demon were aware of the network they could acess with a beast as an ally I feel many demons would pursue a beast. Even if all they could get was a business relationship, it'd be valuable to a demon. On why this would benifit a beast, well though it may not be directly kinship a demon could gift gadgets to share their powers. A demon could also greatly benifit the beasts kin even if not directly the beast itself. <br /> <br /> So in short if they were made aware of what each could offer I feel they would reach out in the interest of business. Even if they never saw each other out side of &quot;working hours&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T18:10:57-07:00","id":867979,"title":"","content":"I'm away from my copy of the first draft and even then, I'm not sure if it's changed, but are Beasts bared from just Soul Pacts or are they bared from Pacts in general? Because if it's the former, than the Beast has a lot to gain from a Demon, and the Unchained could theoretically &quot;harvest&quot; the connections (if not Kinship) the Begotten often have. Or they could softball a Pact in exchange for this thing which is somehow antithetical to the Machine to protect them with the Beast's Compromise-free powers. And if Beasts are immune, just change the one benefiting from the Pact to someone the Beast cares about or who is willing to transfer the assets (if a liquid sort of gift).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}